# Shell scripts must keep LF endings regardless of core.autocrlf — a CRLF
# shebang line becomes "#!/bin/sh\r", which breaks when run on Linux (the
# kernel looks for a literal "/bin/sh\r" interpreter and reports "not
# found" even though the file exists and is executable). Hit this exact
# bug on coginiwattcustomer's deploy/docker-entrypoint.sh; these scripts
# are scp'd straight to the dev VM the same way, so they're exposed to it
# too.
*.sh text eol=lf
